<!-- 18 Appendix: questions -->
<section class="slide">
  <div class="kicker">Appendix &middot; questions a judge might ask</div>
  <h1>Questions we would answer on stage</h1>
  <p class="lead">The online track has no live Q&amp;A, so here are the questions we expect, answered from our own measurements.</p>
  {% set others = tune | rejectattr("id", "equalto", final.id) | list %}{% set fin_t = (tune | selectattr("id", "equalto", final.id) | list | first) %}
  <div class="grid3" style="gap:14px;margin-top:4px">
    <div class="card"><h3>Why not join both cards for one larger model?</h3>
      <p>The job needs two different models at once: a text model and a vision model. One per card keeps both resident and lets them work on the same page in parallel.
      A larger text model was not more accurate here: on held-out pages the best Qwen3 (14B, 30B-A3B) reached {{ "%.1f"|format((others | map(attribute="v2r") | max)*100) if others else "" }}&nbsp;% recall vs. {{ "%.1f"|format(fin_t.v2r*100) if fin_t else "" }}&nbsp;% for gpt-oss-20b. We did not test a two-card (TP&nbsp;=&nbsp;2) model.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Why not Azure AI Language in its offline container?</h3>
      <p>The disconnected container needs an access application and a commitment plan, and it reads text: scanned pages need separate OCR, signatures and seals are out of scope,
      and nothing checks whether a person can still be identified. RedactAgent does all of this in one appliance.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>All test pages are synthetic. Why trust it?</h3>
      <p>Real patient records cannot be used without approval. To limit our own bias, v3 was generated before any result and never used for tuning, v2 added new document types and phone photos,
      and degraded scans keep recall &ge;&nbsp;{{ "%.0f"|format((robust_min*100)|round(0,'floor')) if robust_min else "" }}&nbsp;%.{% if real %} On four real public form layouts recall fell to {{ "%.1f"|format(real.all.recall*100) }}&nbsp;%, and the review queue flagged the pages that held the misses.{% endif %} Real documents have not been tested.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>What if it misses something?</h3>
      <p>Nothing is released without a recorded human approval. The review queue starts with risky pages: {% if triage %}the {{ "%.0f"|format(triage.flagged*100) }}&nbsp;% it flags held {{ "%.0f"|format(triage.caught*100) }}&nbsp;% of the misses on development pages{% endif %}.
      Ink the OCR did not read is flagged, and the audit log shows who approved what.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Does it redact too much?</h3>
      <p>Precision is {{ "%.1f"|format(fin.v3.D_agentic.precision*100) }}&nbsp;% on unseen pages{% if hosp %} ({{ "%.1f"|format(hosp.v3.hospital.D_agentic.precision*100) }}&nbsp;% on hospital documents){% endif %}{% if real %}, {{ "%.1f"|format(real.all.precision*100) }}&nbsp;% on the real form layouts, mostly hospital switchboard numbers and red form lines{% endif %}. The reviewer removes a wrong box with one click,
      and purpose policies keep what a use allows, such as the parties in a court filing.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Does it need the B70?</h3>
      <p>The code talks to any OpenAI-compatible server; Stage I ran on a laptop with Ollama at about 2 pages per minute. The B70 host keeps both models resident and reaches
      {{ "%.1f"|format(best.pages_per_min) if best else "" }} pages per minute: fast enough for a hospital's backlog on one machine.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="foot"><span>Sources: eval/tune3/, eval/robustness/, eval/triage/, docs/MARKET_RESEARCH.md, docs/INTEGRATION.md.</span><span></span></div>
</section>

